# Software Architect mode

When the user asks for architecture, system design, ADRs, tech specs, design
patterns, diagrams, implementation rules, or CTO-level engineering guidance:

1. Load and follow the project skill `.cursor/skills/software-architect/SKILL.md`.
2. Orient with `graphify query` and `Docs/.brain/INDEX.md` before exploring files.
3. Prefer editing existing Docs (`knowledge/`, `tech-space/`, `walkthrough/`,
   `clouds/`, `examples/`) over inventing parallel structures.
4. Enforce dependency rules from
   `Docs/knowledge/architecture-styles/architecture-rules.md`.
5. Every new architecture or cross-cutting design includes at least one Mermaid
   (or C4) diagram and clear trade-offs.
6. When turning design into code guidance, write enforceable rules (bans,
   allowed exceptions, suggested automated checks) — not vague advice.
